Subject: [PATCH] avutil/arm: add bounded ARMv7 NEON NAL start-code search

ARMv7 counterpart to the NAL search introduced by FFmpeg PR #21475:
https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/21475
Applies after 0009-pr21475-aarch64-neon-nal-search.patch on master
 e0e6ca1e29ef3f6b1e9b7d8656fe341eee8cf647.

Reuse the shared API, scalar fallback, and once-only CPU dispatch. Skip
16-byte blocks without adjacent zero bytes, retaining a
last-byte-zero candidate for pairs crossing blocks. Reuse the existing
bounded four-byte C scanner for candidates and tails. The measured short
64-byte cases use C directly. This avoids byte-by-byte candidate scanning
and its regressions on isolated zeros and zero-heavy inputs. Only
caller-saved registers are used; Cortex-A8, Thumb-2, and Android softfp are
supported. No public header or API changes.
diff --git a/libavutil/arm/Makefile b/libavutil/arm/Makefile
index 2988df0..5051661 100644
--- a/libavutil/arm/Makefile
+++ b/libavutil/arm/Makefile
@@ -8,3 +8,4 @@ VFP-OBJS += arm/float_dsp_init_vfp.o                                    \
 
 NEON-OBJS += arm/float_dsp_init_neon.o                                  \
              arm/float_dsp_neon.o                                       \
+             arm/nal.o                                                  \
diff --git a/libavutil/arm/nal.S b/libavutil/arm/nal.S
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b03abce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavutil/arm/nal.S
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+/*
+ * ARM NEON NAL start-code search
+ *
+ * This file is part of FFmpeg.
+ *
+ * FFmpeg is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
